</surname><given-names>RP</given-names></name><name><surname>Pearson</surname><given-names>TA</given-names></name><name><surname>Beller</surname><given-names>GA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Demographics and cardiology, 1950&#x02013;2050</article-title><source>J Am Coll Cardiol.</source><year>2000</year><volume>35</volume><fpage>1067</fpage><lpage>1081</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0735-1097(00)00561-1</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Foot DK, Lewis RP, Pearson TA, Beller GA. Demographics and cardiology, 1950&#x02013;2050. J Am Coll Cardiol. 2000;35:1067&#x02013;81. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10732909</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR9"><label>9.</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Boyce</surname><given-names>ST</given-names></name></person-group><source>The Rochester Community Physician Workforce: Factors Affecting Recruitment and Retention</source><year>2003</year><publisher-loc>Rochester, NY</publisher-loc><publisher-name>CGR</publisher-name></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Boyce ST. The Rochester Community Physician Workforce: Factors Affecting Recruitment and Retention. Rochester, NY: CGR; 2003. </citation></ref><ref id="CR10"><label>10.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Angus</surname><given-names>DC</given-names></name><name><surname>Kelly</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Schmitz</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name><name><surname>White</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Popovich</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Current and projected workforce requirements for care of the critically ill and patients with pulmonary disease: can we meet the requirements of an aging population?</article-title><source>JAMA</source><year>2000</year><volume>284</volume><fpa